{"id": "section-body-05026", "title": "Second-line ART in Adults and Adolescents", "chapterId": "chapter-six", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "MANAGEMENT OF HIV AND AIDS", "Management of Adult and Adolescent Living with HIV with Antiretroviral Therapy", "Second-line ART in Adults and Adolescents"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-05026", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Second-line ART in Adults and Adolescents", "runs": [{"text": "Second-line"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ART"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Adults"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Adolescents"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1741"}}, {"id": "body-05027", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A combination of a Protease Inhibitor (PI) and at least one new NRTI not previously used in first-line therapy are recommended for second-line treatment for adults and adolescents PLHIV aged 15 and above, as shown in Table 6.3. Lamivudine (3TC) or Emtricitabine (FTC) should be continued in subsequent regimens as it lowers viral fitness and increases susceptibility to AZT.", "runs": [{"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "combination"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Protease"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Inhibitor"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PI)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "least"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "one"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "new"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "NRTI"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "previously"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "used"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "first-line"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therapy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "recommended for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "second-line"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "treatment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "f